{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "# Compact CNN: learning digit features\n\n    Lab 2 · MNIST · PyTorch · Google Colab T4\n\n    **Goal.** Train a compact convolutional baseline from scratch, with explicit convolution, pooling and fully connected layers.\n\n   
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 1. Configuration and Drive storage\n\n    One seeded run, one GPU. Seeds and deterministic cuDNN settings improve repeatability; bitwise equality across software and hardware versions is not guaranteed. Record package versions with the results.\n",
   "id": "cell-001"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": "MODEL_KEY = 'cnn'\nCONFIG = {'input_size': 28, 'channels': 1, 'mean': [0.1307], 'std': [0.3081], 'batch_size': 128, 'max_epochs': 20, 'patience': 4, 'optimizer': 'Adam', 'learning_rate': 0.001, 'weight_decay': 0.0001, 'augmentation': {'rotation_degrees': 8, 'translation_fraction': 0.05}, 'architecture': 'conv16-pool-conv32-pool-conv64-global_average_pool-linear10'}\n\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport copy, csv, hashlib, json, math, os, platform, random, time\nimport numpy as np\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nimport torch\nfrom torch import nn\nfrom torch.utils.data import DataLoader, Subset\nimport torchvision\nfrom torchvision import datasets, transforms\nfrom sklearn.metrics import accuracy_score, classification_report, confusion_matrix, ConfusionMatrixDisplay, f1_score\nfrom tqdm.auto import tqdm\n\nif not torch.cuda.is_available():\n    raise RuntimeError('Select Runtime > Change runtime type > T4 GPU, then reconnect.')\nDEVICE = torch.device('cuda:0')\nSEED = 42\nrandom.seed(SEED)\nnp.random.seed(SEED)\ntorch.manual_seed(SEED)\ntorch.cuda.manual_seed_all(SEED)\ntorch.backends.cudnn.benchmark = False\ntorch.backends.cudnn.deterministic = True\n\nfrom google.colab import drive\ndrive.mount('/content/drive')\nPROJECT = Path('/content/drive/MyDrive/Atelier2_MNIST')\nRUN_DIR = PROJECT / 'runs' / MODEL_KEY\nRUN_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\nLOCAL_DATA = Path('/content/mnist_data')\nCONFIG['seed'] = SEED\nCONFIG['gpu_name'] = torch.cuda.get_device_name(0)\nCONFIG['gpu_count_used'] = 1\nCONFIG['torch_version'] = str(torch.__version__)\nCONFIG['torchvision_version'] = str(torchvision.__version__)\nCONFIG['python_version'] = platform.python_version()\nprint('GPU:', CONFIG['gpu_name'])\nprint('Outputs:', RUN_DIR)\n\ndef write_json(path, value):\n    path = Path(path)\n    temporary = path.with_suffix(path.suffix + '.tmp')\n    temporary.write_text(json.dumps(value, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False))\n    os.replace(temporary, path)\n\ndef atomic_torch_save(value, path):\n    path = Path(path)\n    temporary = path.with_suffix(path.suffix + '.tmp')\n    torch.save(value, temporary)\n    os.replace(temporary, path)\n\ndef seed_worker(worker_id):\n    worker_seed = torch.initial_seed() % 2**32\n    np.random.seed(worker_seed)\n    random.seed(worker_seed)\n\ndef make_loader(dataset, batch_size, shuffle=False, collate_fn=None):\n    return DataLoader(\n        dataset, batch_size=batch_size, shuffle=shuffle, num_workers=2,\n        pin_memory=True, worker_init_fn=seed_worker,\n        generator=torch.Generator().manual_seed(SEED), collate_fn=collate_fn,\n    )\n\ndef split_digest(train_indices, validation_indices):\n    payload = json.dumps({'train': train_indices, 'validation': validation_indices}, separators=(',', ':'))\n    return hashlib.sha256(payload.encode()).hexdigest()\n",
   "id": "cell-002"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## Download the required MNIST dataset from Kaggle\n\n    The source is exclusively [hojjatk/mnist-dataset](https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/hojjatk/mnist-dataset), as specified by the lab. `kagglehub` downloads its latest version to the Colab runtime cache. Search for the four IDX files, decompress `.gz` files if needed, and verify magic numbers, image dimensions, counts and file lengths. Save file fingerprints in Drive so the exact data can be checked across runs. There is no fallback to another MNIST download source.\n",
   "id": "cell-003"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": "# Kaggle is the only MNIST download source. Torchvision will read local IDX files.\nimport gzip\nimport importlib.metadata\nimport shutil\nimport struct\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\ntry:\n    import kagglehub\nexcept ModuleNotFoundError:\n    subprocess.check_call([sys.executable, '-m', 'pip', 'install', '--quiet', 'kagglehub'])\n    import kagglehub\n\nDATASET_HANDLE = 'hojjatk/mnist-dataset'\npath = kagglehub.dataset_download(DATASET_HANDLE)\nprint('Path to dataset files:', path)\ndataset_path = Path(path)\nraw_directory = LOCAL_DATA / 'MNIST' / 'raw'\nraw_directory.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n\ndef validate_idx_file(file_path, magic, expected_count):\n    # Validate the decompressed IDX header and exact payload size before loading.\n    with Path(file_path).open('rb') as file:\n        header = file.read(8)\n        if len(header) != 8:\n            raise ValueError(f'Truncated IDX header: {file_path}')\n        actual_magic, count = struct.unpack('>II', header)\n        if actual_magic != magic or count != expected_count:\n            raise ValueError(f'Unexpected IDX magic/count in {file_path}: {actual_magic}, {count}')\n        if magic == 2051:\n            dimensions = file.read(8)\n            if len(dimensions) != 8 or struct.unpack('>II', dimensions) != (28, 28):\n                raise ValueError(f'Expected 28x28 images: {file_path}')\n            expected_bytes = 16 + count * 28 * 28\n        else:\n            labels = file.read()\n            if len(labels) != count or any(label > 9 for label in labels):\n                raise ValueError(f'Invalid digit labels: {file_path}')\n            expected_bytes = 8 + count\n    if Path(file_path).stat().st_size != expected_bytes:\n        raise ValueError(f'IDX payload length mismatch: {file_path}')\n\ndef stage_idx_file(source_root, destination_root, filename, magic, count):\n    candidates = sorted(\n        (p for p in Path(source_root).rglob('*') if p.is_file() and p.name in (filename, filename + '.gz')),\n        key=lambda p: (p.suffix == '.gz', str(p)),\n    )\n    if not candidates:\n        raise FileNotFoundError(f'{filename} or {filename}.gz not found in Kaggle dataset {source_root}')\n    source = candidates[0]\n    destination = Path(destination_root) / filename\n    temporary = destination.with_suffix(destination.suffix + '.tmp')\n    try:\n        opener = gzip.open if source.name.endswith('.gz') else open\n        with opener(source, 'rb') as incoming, temporary.open('wb') as outgoing:\n            shutil.copyfileobj(incoming, outgoing)\n        validate_idx_file(temporary, magic, count)\n        os.replace(temporary, destination)\n    finally:\n        temporary.unlink(missing_ok=True)\n    digest = hashlib.sha256()\n    with destination.open('rb') as file:\n        for chunk in iter(lambda: file.read(1024 * 1024), b''):\n            digest.update(chunk)\n    print('Kaggle IDX ready:', filename)\n    return digest.hexdigest()\n\nrequired_files = {\n    'train-images-idx3-ubyte': (2051, 60000),\n    'train-labels-idx1-ubyte': (2049, 60000),\n    't10k-images-idx3-ubyte': (2051, 10000),\n    't10k-labels-idx1-ubyte': (2049, 10000),\n}\ndataset_hashes = {\n    filename: stage_idx_file(dataset_path, raw_directory, filename, magic, count)\n    for filename, (magic, count) in required_files.items()\n}\nCONFIG['dataset_handle'] = DATASET_HANDLE\nCONFIG['dataset_file_sha256'] = dataset_hashes\nCONFIG['kagglehub_version'] = importlib.metadata.version('kagglehub')\nwrite_json(RUN_DIR / 'dataset_provenance.json', {\n    'handle': DATASET_HANDLE, 'download_path': str(dataset_path),\n    'file_sha256': dataset_hashes, 'kagglehub_version': CONFIG['kagglehub_version'],\n})\n",
   "id": "cell-004"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 2. Shared data protocol\n\n    Use 54,000 training images, 6,000 validation images and the untouched official 10,000-image test set. All four new notebooks share exactly the same split indices. Training augmentation applies rotation up to ±8° and translation up to 5%; validation and test have no random augmentation. Three-channel models repeat the grayscale image and use ImageNet normalization; one-channel models use MNIST normalization.\n",
   "id": "cell-005"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": "# The same seeded index assignment is regenerated and checked in all four notebooks.\npermutation = torch.randperm(60000, generator=torch.Generator().manual_seed(SEED)).tolist()\nvalidation_indices = permutation[:6000]\ntrain_indices = permutation[6000:]\nsplit = {'seed': SEED, 'train_indices': train_indices, 'validation_indices': validation_indices,\n         'test': 'official MNIST test split; all 10000 images'}\nsplit_path = PROJECT / 'shared_split.json'\nif split_path.exists():\n    if json.loads(split_path.read_text()) != split:\n        raise RuntimeError('Existing Drive split differs. Use a new project folder rather than overwrite it.')\nelse:\n    write_json(split_path, split)\nassert len(set(train_indices) & set(validation_indices)) == 0\nassert len(set(train_indices + validation_indices)) == 60000\nCONFIG['split_sha256'] = split_digest(train_indices, validation_indices)\nCONFIG['train_size'], CONFIG['validation_size'], CONFIG['test_size'] = 54000, 6000, 10000\n\ndef image_transform(training=False):\n    steps = []\n    if training:\n        steps.append(transforms.RandomAffine(degrees=8, translate=(0.05, 0.05), fill=0))\n    if CONFIG['input_size'] != 28:\n        steps.append(transforms.Resize((CONFIG['input_size'], CONFIG['input_size']), antialias=True))\n    if CONFIG['channels'] == 3:\n        steps.append(transforms.Grayscale(num_output_channels=3))\n    steps.extend([transforms.ToTensor(), transforms.Normalize(CONFIG['mean'], CONFIG['std'])])\n    return transforms.Compose(steps)\n\ntraining_source = datasets.MNIST(LOCAL_DATA, train=True, download=False, transform=image_transform(True))\nvalidation_source = datasets.MNIST(LOCAL_DATA, train=True, download=False, transform=image_transform(False))\ntest_set = datasets.MNIST(LOCAL_DATA, train=False, download=False, transform=image_transform(False))\ntrain_set = Subset(training_source, train_indices)\nvalidation_set = Subset(validation_source, validation_indices)\ntrain_loader = make_loader(train_set, CONFIG['batch_size'], shuffle=True)\nvalidation_loader = make_loader(validation_set, CONFIG['batch_size'])\ntest_loader = make_loader(test_set, CONFIG['batch_size'])\nwrite_json(RUN_DIR / 'config.json', CONFIG)\nprint(f'Train {len(train_set)} | validation {len(validation_set)} | test {len(test_set)}')\n\nimages, labels = next(iter(validation_loader))\nassert images.shape[1:] == (CONFIG['channels'], CONFIG['input_size'], CONFIG['input_size'])\nmean = torch.tensor(CONFIG['mean']).view(-1, 1, 1)\nstd = torch.tensor(CONFIG['std']).view(-1, 1, 1)\nfig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 6, figsize=(12, 2.5))\nfor ax, image, label in zip(axes, images[:6], labels[:6]):\n    display = (image * std + mean).clamp(0, 1)\n    ax.imshow(display[0] if CONFIG['channels'] == 1 else display.permute(1, 2, 0), cmap='gray')\n    ax.set_title(f'Digit {label.item()}'); ax.axis('off')\nplt.tight_layout(); plt.show()\n",
   "id": "cell-006"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 3. Model and optimizer\n\n    Inspect the architecture and parameter counts before training. A shape check below uses validation images only. Learning rates for pretrained layers are smaller than those for newly initialized classifiers.\n",
   "id": "cell-007"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": "class CompactDigitCNN(nn.Module):\n    def __init__(self):\n        super().__init__()\n        def block(in_channels, out_channels, pool=False):\n            layers = [nn.Conv2d(in_channels, out_channels, kernel_size=3, stride=1, padding=1, bias=False),\n                      nn.BatchNorm2d(out_channels), nn.ReLU(inplace=True)]\n            if pool: layers.append(nn.MaxPool2d(kernel_size=2, stride=2))\n            return nn.Sequential(*layers)\n        self.features = nn.Sequential(block(1, 16, True), block(16, 32, True), block(32, 64))\n        self.classifier = nn.Sequential(nn.AdaptiveAvgPool2d(1), nn.Flatten(), nn.Linear(64, 10))\n    def forward(self, images):\n        return self.classifier(self.features(images))\n\nmodel = CompactDigitCNN().to(DEVICE)\noptimizer = torch.optim.Adam(model.parameters(), lr=CONFIG['learning_rate'], weight_decay=CONFIG['weight_decay'])\n\n\nmodel = model.to(DEVICE)\nmodel.eval()\nwith torch.inference_mode():\n    shape = model(images[:2].to(DEVICE)).shape\nassert tuple(shape) == (2, 10), shape\nprint(model)\nprint('Total parameters:', sum(p.numel() for p in model.parameters()))\nprint('Trainable parameters:', sum(p.numel() for p in model.parameters() if p.requires_grad))\n",
   "id": "cell-008"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 4. Train and select on validation\n\n    Cross-entropy receives raw logits. Loss is averaged by the number of images, not by the number of batches. Validation selects checkpoints and controls the scheduler and early stopping; the test loader is not used here.\n\n    Timing includes training, validation and best-checkpoint writes to Drive, but excludes downloads, setup and final test evaluation. The first epoch gives a hardware-specific estimate. Stop once the patience limit is reached and restore the lowest-validation-loss model.\n",
   "id": "cell-009"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": "criterion = nn.CrossEntropyLoss()\nscheduler = torch.optim.lr_scheduler.ReduceLROnPlateau(optimizer, mode='min', factor=0.5, patience=2)\nBEST_PATH = RUN_DIR / 'best_checkpoint.pt'\n\ndef classification_epoch(loader, training=False):\n    model.train(training)\n    loss_sum, correct, samples = 0.0, 0, 0\n    with torch.set_grad_enabled(training):\n        for images, labels in tqdm(loader, leave=False, desc='Train' if training else 'Validation'):\n            images = images.to(DEVICE, non_blocking=True)\n            labels = labels.to(DEVICE, non_blocking=True)\n            if training:\n                optimizer.zero_grad(set_to_none=True)\n            logits = model(images)\n            loss = criterion(logits, labels)\n            if training:\n                loss.backward()\n                torch.nn.utils.clip_grad_norm_(model.parameters(), max_norm=1.0)\n                optimizer.step()\n            loss_sum += loss.item() * len(labels)\n            correct += (logits.argmax(1) == labels).sum().item()\n            samples += len(labels)\n    return loss_sum / samples, correct / samples\n\n# Prevent accidental replacement of a completed experiment. Change this explicitly for a fresh run.\nOVERWRITE_RUN = False\nif (RUN_DIR / 'history.json').exists() and not OVERWRITE_RUN:\n    raise RuntimeError('This run already has a history. Load its checkpoint for evaluation, or explicitly enable OVERWRITE_RUN.')\n# If explicitly restarting, do not let previous metrics survive a new or interrupted training run.\nfor stale_file in ['metrics.json', 'predictions.csv', 'test_evaluation_started.json']:\n    (RUN_DIR / stale_file).unlink(missing_ok=True)\n\nbest_loss, best_epoch, stale_epochs = float('inf'), None, 0\nhistory = []\ntraining_seconds = 0.0\nfor epoch in range(1, CONFIG['max_epochs'] + 1):\n    torch.cuda.synchronize()\n    start = time.perf_counter()\n    train_loss, train_accuracy = classification_epoch(train_loader, training=True)\n    validation_loss, validation_accuracy = classification_epoch(validation_loader)\n    scheduler.step(validation_loss)\n    improved = validation_loss < best_loss\n    if improved:\n        best_loss, best_epoch, stale_epochs = validation_loss, epoch, 0\n        atomic_torch_save({'model_state': model.state_dict(), 'epoch': epoch,\n                          'validation_loss': validation_loss, 'config': CONFIG}, BEST_PATH)\n    else:\n        stale_epochs += 1\n    torch.cuda.synchronize()\n    epoch_seconds = time.perf_counter() - start\n    training_seconds += epoch_seconds\n    history.append({'epoch': epoch, 'train_loss': train_loss, 'train_accuracy': train_accuracy,\n                    'validation_loss': validation_loss, 'validation_accuracy': validation_accuracy,\n                    'epoch_seconds': epoch_seconds, 'training_seconds': training_seconds,\n                    'learning_rates': [g['lr'] for g in optimizer.param_groups], 'best_epoch': best_epoch})\n    write_json(RUN_DIR / 'history.json', history)\n    print(f'Epoch {epoch:02d}: train loss {train_loss:.4f}, val loss {validation_loss:.4f}, '\n          f'val accuracy {validation_accuracy:.2%}, time {epoch_seconds:.1f}s')\n    if epoch == 1:\n        print(f'First-epoch estimate for {CONFIG[\"max_epochs\"]} epochs: '\n              f'{epoch_seconds * CONFIG[\"max_epochs\"] / 60:.1f} min; early stopping may shorten it.')\n    if stale_epochs >= CONFIG['patience']:\n        print('Early stopping.'); break\n\ncheckpoint = torch.load(BEST_PATH, map_location=DEVICE, weights_only=True)\nmodel.load_state_dict(checkpoint['model_state'])\nmodel.eval()\nprint(f'Best epoch: {checkpoint[\"epoch\"]}; total training/validation/checkpoint time: {training_seconds / 60:.2f} min')\n",
   "id": "cell-010"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 5. Final held-out evaluation\n\n    Run once after training. Save accuracy, macro F1, correctly weighted mean test loss, prediction labels and per-class scores. If this cell was interrupted, inspect saved files before explicitly allowing a repeat. Do not use test results to select new hyperparameters for this reported run.\n",
   "id": "cell-011"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": "# This cell can also evaluate an existing checkpoint after rerunning setup, data and model cells.\ncheckpoint = torch.load(RUN_DIR / 'best_checkpoint.pt', map_location=DEVICE, weights_only=True)\nif checkpoint['config'] != CONFIG:\n    raise RuntimeError('Checkpoint configuration differs from this notebook configuration.')\nmodel.load_state_dict(checkpoint['model_state'])\nmodel.eval()\nhistory = json.loads((RUN_DIR / 'history.json').read_text())\nALLOW_REPEAT_TEST = False\nif (RUN_DIR / 'test_evaluation_started.json').exists() and not ALLOW_REPEAT_TEST:\n    raise RuntimeError('Test evaluation was already started. Read saved metrics, or explicitly enable a repeated evaluation.')\nwrite_json(RUN_DIR / 'test_evaluation_started.json', {'best_epoch': checkpoint['epoch']})\n\ntargets, predictions = [], []\ntest_loss_sum = 0.0\ntorch.cuda.synchronize(); evaluation_start = time.perf_counter()\nwith torch.inference_mode():\n    for images, labels in tqdm(test_loader, desc='Final test'):\n        logits = model(images.to(DEVICE, non_blocking=True))\n        test_loss_sum += nn.functional.cross_entropy(\n            logits, labels.to(DEVICE, non_blocking=True), reduction='sum').item()\n        predictions.extend(logits.argmax(1).cpu().tolist())\n        targets.extend(labels.tolist())\ntorch.cuda.synchronize()\nmetrics = {\n    'model': MODEL_KEY, 'source': 'new_colab_run', 'accuracy': accuracy_score(targets, predictions),\n    'f1_macro': f1_score(targets, predictions, labels=list(range(10)), average='macro', zero_division=0),\n    'test_loss': test_loss_sum / len(targets), 'loss_type': 'mean cross entropy per image',\n    'training_seconds': sum(row['epoch_seconds'] for row in history),\n    'timing_scope': 'training + validation + scheduler + best checkpoint writes; excludes setup and final test',\n    'evaluation_seconds': time.perf_counter() - evaluation_start,\n    'epochs_executed': len(history), 'best_epoch': checkpoint['epoch'], 'test_size': len(targets),\n    'gpu_name': CONFIG['gpu_name'], 'gpu_count_used': 1, 'seed': SEED,\n    'train_size': len(train_set), 'validation_size': len(validation_set),\n    'split_sha256': CONFIG['split_sha256'],\n    'dataset_handle': CONFIG['dataset_handle'], 'dataset_file_sha256': CONFIG['dataset_file_sha256'],\n    'total_parameters': sum(p.numel() for p in model.parameters()),\n    'trainable_parameters': sum(p.numel() for p in model.parameters() if p.requires_grad),\n}\nassert len(targets) == 10000\nwrite_json(RUN_DIR / 'metrics.json', metrics)\nwith (RUN_DIR / 'predictions.csv').open('w', newline='') as file:\n    writer = csv.writer(file); writer.writerow(['test_index', 'true_digit', 'predicted_digit'])\n    writer.writerows((i, t, p) for i, (t, p) in enumerate(zip(targets, predictions)))\nreport = classification_report(targets, predictions, labels=list(range(10)), digits=4, zero_division=0)\n(RUN_DIR / 'classification_report.txt').write_text(report)\nprint(json.dumps(metrics, indent=2)); print(report)\n",
   "id": "cell-012"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 6. Curves, confusion matrix and examples\n\n    These plots read saved results. They do not perform additional test inference. Examples show four initial test images followed by up to four errors. No test-loss curve is drawn because the test set is evaluated only at the end.\n",
   "id": "cell-013"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": "# Reload persisted results: rerunning this cell does not evaluate the model on the test set again.\nhistory = json.loads((RUN_DIR / 'history.json').read_text())\nwith (RUN_DIR / 'predictions.csv').open() as file:\n    rows = list(csv.DictReader(file))\ntargets = [int(row['true_digit']) for row in rows]\npredictions = [int(row['predicted_digit']) for row in rows]\nfig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(12, 4))\nepochs = [row['epoch'] for row in history]\nfor prefix, title in [('train', 'Training'), ('validation', 'Validation')]:\n    axes[0].plot(epochs, [row[prefix + '_loss'] for row in history], label=title)\n    axes[1].plot(epochs, [row[prefix + '_accuracy'] for row in history], label=title)\nfor ax, label in zip(axes, ['Cross-entropy loss', 'Accuracy']):\n    ax.set_xlabel('Epoch'); ax.set_ylabel(label); ax.legend(); ax.grid(alpha=0.3)\nfig.tight_layout(); fig.savefig(RUN_DIR / 'learning_curves.png', dpi=160); plt.show()\n\nfig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(8, 7))\nConfusionMatrixDisplay(confusion_matrix(targets, predictions, labels=list(range(10))), display_labels=range(10)).plot(ax=ax, cmap='Blues', colorbar=False)\nax.set_title(MODEL_KEY + ' — final test predictions')\nfig.tight_layout(); fig.savefig(RUN_DIR / 'confusion_matrix.png', dpi=160); plt.show()\n\nerror_indices = [i for i, (t, p) in enumerate(zip(targets, predictions)) if t != p]\nexample_indices = list(range(4)) + error_indices[:4]\nraw_test = datasets.MNIST(LOCAL_DATA, train=False, download=False)\nfig, axes = plt.subplots(1, len(example_indices), figsize=(2.1 * len(example_indices), 2.8), squeeze=False)\nfor ax, index in zip(axes.flat, example_indices):\n    image, label = raw_test[index]\n    predicted = predictions[index]\n    ax.imshow(image, cmap='gray'); ax.axis('off')\n    ax.set_title(f'True: {label} | Pred: {predicted}', color='green' if predicted == label else 'red', fontsize=9)\nfig.tight_layout(); fig.savefig(RUN_DIR / 'prediction_examples.png', dpi=160); plt.show()\n",
   "id": "cell-014"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 7. Update the cross-model comparison\n\n    Run this cell again after completing another notebook. Missing experiments remain blank. Original Faster R-CNN scores are explicitly historical, with their original two-GPU configuration and known evaluation limitations; they are not outputs of corrected code.\n",
   "id": "cell-015"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
